.TH PKG-INSTALL 1 "2026-08-07" "pkg-install" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pkg-install \- interactive package installer (fzf TUI)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkg-install
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pkg-install
is an interactive
.BR fzf (1)
front end for installing packages from the enabled sync repositories.
It takes no command\-line arguments; the whole workflow happens inside the
fzf list and its preview pane.
.P
On start, the script snapshots the set of installed packages
(\fBpacman \-Qq\fR) into a temporary lookup table and lists every package
available in the configured repositories (\fBpacman \-Slq\fR). Each entry
is prefixed with a state marker:
.IP \(bu 2
\fB★\fR
the package is already installed
.IP \(bu 2
\fB○\fR
the package is available but not installed
.P
Filter by typing, toggle entries into the selection with
.B Tab
and press Enter. The chosen package names are collected and installed in
a single call to
.BR paru (1)
(\fBparu \-S \-\-noconfirm\fR), so no further confirmation is asked. If the
selection is empty (the list is dismissed), the script exits silently
without making any change.
.P
A wrap\-enabled preview pane at the bottom (65% of the screen) shows
detailed information for the highlighted package via
.BR pacman (8)
(\fBpacman \-Sii\fR, using field \fB{2}\fR, the package name after the
state marker). The pointer and multi\-select marker are shown in green,
and the preview label reads:
.IP
\fBalt\-p: toggle preview | alt\-j/k: scroll preview | tab: multi\-select\fR
.SS Key bindings
.IP \(bu 2
.B Tab
toggle multi\-selection of the current entry
.IP \(bu 2
.B Ctrl-J
move the cursor down the list
.IP \(bu 2
.B Ctrl-K
move the cursor up the list
.IP \(bu 2
.B Alt-P
toggle the preview pane
.IP \(bu 2
.B Alt-D
scroll the preview half a page down
.IP \(bu 2
.B Alt-U
scroll the preview half a page up
.IP \(bu 2
.B Alt-J
scroll the preview one line down
.IP \(bu 2
.B Alt-K
scroll the preview one line up
.P
The script requires
.BR fzf (1)
and
.BR paru (1);
package listing and installed\-state detection use
.BR pacman (8).
.SH EXAMPLES
Install one or more packages:
.IP
.EX
pkg-install
.EE
.P
Type a search term to filter, press
.B Tab
on each package of interest, then press Enter to install all of them.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR paru (1),
.BR pacman (8),
.BR fzf (1),
.BR pkg-install-aur (1),
.BR pkg-remove.sh (1)
